{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","created_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1e355114c7f4dddfb5ff7e443dc39b4cab3f8258f3d728e1b89f32bc479575ac","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"joinwell52-ai/joinwell52@6961492e9a46 snapshot 2a0fd4110d4ba967","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ff8beeb2e6ec35ebf26448c47e90c9e866735ea43f56604af6b76ff05d6e8b6e"],"source_ids":["src_271ed53826255b5cbaeebe08203a3d06"],"text":"The Reference Reader is run via npm commands: `npm run demo` for a demo delivery and `npm run tmpa:s1.0:conformance` for the conformance runner, after `npm ci`.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","updated_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","created_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.5,"id":"clm_3e31c5f0a4bbea1e40c124148c226af688e9c08542ed25fee4498cb922070261","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=inference; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"joinwell52-ai/joinwell52@6961492e9a46 snapshot 2a0fd4110d4ba967","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_680bc19fd69496371d8e26b5976b935b3990415fff3a0866428c7f91057cf5c2"],"source_ids":["src_d161b6a674b455f6afb2c1d9df22a5f2"],"text":"The draft proposes each execution role be bounded by a default-deny Capability Envelope/Sandbox Boundary limiting tools, paths, network, and credentials, plus a negative list of contextual business rules; as draft target language, this is not confirmed shipped behavior.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","updated_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","created_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.5,"id":"clm_4a97376aef4eefa62aeee9c2e99b5df6e46f3f6422599db7dfd9713e10998356","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=inference; facet=orchestration","setting":"joinwell52-ai/joinwell52@6961492e9a46 snapshot 2a0fd4110d4ba967","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_562c7103783ad80e06b0b59bb8a4534cd491bbe8091c14a91781244586a0532b","slc_b9d27a0d7960d81af4fa2f297a02ed96d1063354aa7ee5c7521229473e3461f6","slc_fd7a528184779edcff89fa369fbef22cd34be7c184dc7ad9e93a637aa3ba3ae4"],"source_ids":["src_d161b6a674b455f6afb2c1d9df22a5f2"],"text":"The V0.3.1 draft architecture proposes a five-layer design (FCoP fact layer, TMPA Reader, Runtime, definition/deployment, instance) coordinated by asynchronous fact loops rather than a synchronous all-agents-online pipeline; it is explicitly a draft, not a stable specification.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","updated_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","created_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4de9770974b0254a0a0ed211da8c8565f72ba084a182930944c608dd51275970","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"joinwell52-ai/joinwell52@6961492e9a46 snapshot 2a0fd4110d4ba967","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3d84bab95921a6bc0b020f05086173221f04f856d814b0ce31f49805bfc26541","slc_47756b8914a3d5ce5c7f83b3510d7944df309847bac19ac711eaa336c6e9ee45"],"source_ids":["src_271ed53826255b5cbaeebe08203a3d06"],"text":"CodeFlowMu is described as a local PM/DEV/QA/OPS AI development team with a PC control center and a mobile PWA, distributed as a proprietary free Windows x64 preview from a separate distribution repository.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","updated_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","created_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_70f0d211a2a28b9d6d691a6f3a75fc2899ff1d96afde2b3540e15befcf9f94d7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"joinwell52-ai/joinwell52@6961492e9a46 snapshot 2a0fd4110d4ba967","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_38de0e8f11129a1c8b08d3713acdd8307a0e7996bc5ec4096e03efbcc7eaf6c2"],"source_ids":["src_271ed53826255b5cbaeebe08203a3d06"],"text":"TMPA moves durable work facts out of volatile model memory so lifecycle, authority, conflict, and audit state can be reconstructed from inspectable evidence across asynchronous execution.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","updated_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","created_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_791a18214cb198bbbfee43aa9b7ee246f17004f7f906430224b8694d8328d89f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"joinwell52-ai/joinwell52@6961492e9a46 snapshot 2a0fd4110d4ba967","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_403b5bca211989c48eeb9e725a5d6f0163049a1a51fe13331f67f2762900f9c6","slc_d1650279f4c5a2f82b8e354e616577d7175fb89632cbcd245fe67914b3640dd1"],"source_ids":["src_271ed53826255b5cbaeebe08203a3d06"],"text":"The recorded conformance result is 14 PASS / 0 PARTIAL / 0 NOT RUN / 0 FAIL for the S1.0 criteria, alongside reported suite results such as 71/71 mandatory assertions and a 1,522-pass CodeFlowMu runtime suite.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","updated_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","created_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_80fdef812d27637c00c822c5d8d81bdcff9109dbf0abffafa2ea65236e7c0205","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"joinwell52-ai/joinwell52@6961492e9a46 snapshot 2a0fd4110d4ba967","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ee7578214a44061e03fa5c39117eb078cc42cdfdbdf0b03b5e896d876236662a"],"source_ids":["src_271ed53826255b5cbaeebe08203a3d06"],"text":"The README states the conformance evidence is author-run for one exact implementation revision and input bundle, and is not independent certification, universal conformance, or proof hallucinations are eliminated.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:01:16Z","updated_by_operation":"op_18b71226099e42d08c25425e20711357"}
